  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "A group of 12 people met at a café for lunch. Each person had a pie or chips or both.\nIf 9 people had a pie and 7 had chips, find the probability that one of the people:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "had chips, given that this person had a pie",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{9}$",
          "worked": "A Venn diagram is useful here. Let $P$ be the set of people who had a pie and $C$ the set who had chips.\n$$\\begin{align*}|P\\cap C|&=9+7-12\\\\&=4\\\\\\Pr(C\\mid P)&=\\frac{|P\\cap C|}{|P|}\\\\&=\\frac{4}{9}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "did not have a pie given that the person had chips.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{7}$",
          "worked": "Let $P$ be the set of people who had a pie and $C$ the set who had chips.\n$$\\begin{align*}|P\\cap C|&=9+7-12\\\\&=4\\\\|P'\\cap C|&=7-4\\\\&=3\\\\\\Pr(P'\\mid C)&=\\frac{|P'\\cap C|}{|C|}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n$P'\\cap C$ means chips only.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
